  "description": "Change of Use from Class C3 (single residential dwelling) to Use Class C4 (HMO) Retrospective",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The original dwelling had a gross internal floor space which fails to meet the standard of 120 square metres, thereby resulted in the unacceptable loss of a much needed family home within the Borough, contrary to Policy 8(i) of the Havering Local Plan 2021.",
    "The intensification of the site is likely to generate high levels of activity and results in an unacceptable impact on neighbouring residential occupiers in terms of noise and general disturbance associated with the HMO use contrary to Policies 7 and 8 of the Havering Local Plan 2021.",
    "A bedroom and the kitchen is insufficient in size, there is no communal living or dining area and a room would be more than floor away from the kitchen which is harmful to the amenity of the occupiers of the HMO contrary to Policies 7 and 8 of the Havering Local Plan.",
    "it is considered that the development is likely to result in an increased parking congestion in surrounding streets, contrary to Policies 8 and 24 of the Havering Local Plan and the guidance contained in the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Statement Required by Article 35 (2) of the Town and Country Planning (Development Management Procedure) (England) Order 2015: Consideration was given to seeking amendments, but given conflict with adopted planning policy and time limits, amendments were not sought."
  ],
